 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "The picture printed on a sheet of rubber stretched across the frame. Whatever moves in the shot grabs the sheet and drags it along: a walker pulls a stretched dent of the background with them, a passing car tugs the road behind it, and once they are gone the sheet snaps back past its rest and wobbles flat. Camera moves are left out, so only the things moving in the scene pull. A still shot stays exactly as it was.",
